---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy - The Whetstone"
  description="How The Whetstone handles your data."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <main class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-6 pt-16 pb-24">

    <nav class="mb-10">
      <a href="/" class="text-xs text-muted hover:text-ink transition-colors">← The Whetstone</a>
    </nav>

    <header class="mb-10">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-accent uppercase mb-3">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink-strong mb-4">How we handle your data</h1>
      <p class="text-muted text-sm">Last updated 26 May 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-sm text-ink leading-relaxed">

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-accent uppercase mb-3">The short version</h2>
        <p>
          No analytics. No tracking cookies. No advertising. We do not sell, share, or profile your data.
          The only information that leaves your device is the text you submit for analysis, and that is
          sent straight to an AI provider under a zero-data-retention agreement - it is not stored or
          used to train models.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-accent uppercase mb-3">What we store</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          We store almost nothing. The only server-side state is an IP-keyed daily quota counter held in
          Cloudflare KV. It records how many API requests a given IP address has made in the current
          24-hour window so we can enforce the free-tier rate limit. The counter expires automatically
          at midnight UTC and is never linked to any personal identifier beyond the IP address itself.
        </p>
        <p>
          Published Logic Scorecards (question, positions, analysis) are stored in Cloudflare KV so the
          public pages can render them. Scorecards contain no personal data - they are editorial content
          created by the site curator.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-accent uppercase mb-3">AI providers</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          When you submit text for analysis, it is forwarded to Google Gemini under Google's
          <strong class="font-semibold text-ink-strong">Zero Data Retention</strong> policy for the
          Gemini API. This means Google does not store your input or output, and the content is not
          used to improve Google's models. You can read Google's terms at
          <a href="https://cloud.google.com/terms/data-processing-terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent hover:underline">cloud.google.com/terms/data-processing-terms</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not use the Anthropic API for public requests at this time. If that changes, this page
          will be updated.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-accent uppercase mb-3">Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          We set no tracking or analytics cookies. The site does not use any third-party scripts
          (no Google Analytics, no Meta Pixel, no ad networks). Your browser may cache static assets
          as normal HTTP caching - that is not a cookie.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-accent uppercase mb-3">Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Because we collect no personal data beyond ephemeral IP-based counters, there is nothing to
          request, correct, or delete. If you have a question or concern, email
          <a href="mailto:daniel.livingstone44@gmail.com" class="text-accent hover:underline">daniel.livingstone44@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>

  </main>
</Base>
